{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492364-dark-age-mage-|-foundation-s-speciality-and-aura","id":1492364,"title":"Dark Age - Mage | Foundation's speciality and Aura","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-05T07:57:04-07:00","id":1492364,"title":"Dark Age - Mage | Foundation's speciality and Aura","content":"As you understand, I read Mage - dark ages. The same ones with pillars.<br /> <br /> No matter how I look, I can't find the information for 2 questions.<br /> <br /> 1) Specializations of the Foundation. How does this specialization work? Do I get them at level 4 and 5 or at level 2? Or, if I specialize in movement and stealth - Do I get a certain bonus (another success) to move, for every 10 rolled in Dex+Athletics? Or does it only affect movement magic (acceleration, distance change)?<br /> <br /> #### OK I found Spec in DAM - Grimoire ####<br /> <br /> 2) Aura. Are aura modifiers a narrative part? Is there a certain mechanic here? If I'm F-5 and have a holy pious priest aura, do I just add my Foundation on the piety check? Or do I just roll my Foundation instead and use it on check as an extra success?<br /> <br /> #### I found Aura in DAM ####","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 09-08-2022, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T03:34:13-07:00","id":1492499,"title":"","content":"Sorry for waiting long <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a> , been busy and had to reread DA. Mage and DA:Vampire, but:<br /> <br /> 1) It's like any other speciality, you gain it at Dot 4, and it applies to any rolls involving that trait - that means whenever you roll your Foundation where it applies (so only on magic rolls most of the time)<br /> <br /> 2) Aura modifiers are both mechanical and narrative, each of the Fellowships has a specific Aura in their writeup, and the higher their Foundation is the more it affects them (+/- 0-3). The Aura makes other people feel their specific type of disconnection from normalcy for better or for worse. Depending on if it might be useful or not it will increase or decrease difficulties on social rolls. It doesn't affect magic itself as it only applies to social rolls.<br /> <br /> So for instance the Aura of the Messianic Voices is Glory - They always appear devout and holy. So if a Mage of the Voices with Foundation 4 is trying to infiltrate a smuggling operation or a cult all his social difficulties will be at +2... however if he is trying to ingratiate himself with the local bishop or gain access to the reliquiary his social difficulties would be at -2 difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T09:51:11-07:00","id":1492525,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I got the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 09-07-2022, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T22:01:27-07:00","id":1492570,"title":"","content":"Basically, Aura is the Dark Ages Mage counterpart to the Resonance traits from MRev.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T01:14:49-07:00","id":1492577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492364-dark-age-mage-|-foundation-s-speciality-and-aura?p=1492570#post1492570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, Aura is the Dark Ages Mage counterpart to the Resonance traits from MRev.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way yes, but they mapped it out by the DA: Vampire rules for what being near a person with a very high or very low road feels like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}